\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Example}
\title{An exact dressed pair and cyclic loop mean}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{In the rational sign model of \ref{fdip-00UA}, take
#{x=(0,0)}, #{y=(1,0)} and let #{\gamma:y\to x}
traverse the reverse of the tree edge from #{x} to
#{y}. Use the identity insertion on the rank-one
fiber and the barred-first product
##{P_\gamma(U)=\bar\psi_{00}h_\gamma(U)\psi_{10}.}
Then the normalized coupled values are
##{\langle P_\gamma\rangle
  =\frac{412470750}{35803094657},\qquad
 \langle L_1(\,\cdot\,;00)\rangle
  =-\frac{330765108}{35803094657}.}
The first number is the value of the specified
dressed pair, with its ordering and its chosen path.}

\p{In the spanning-tree representatives of
\ref{fdip-00UA}, #{h_\gamma=1}. Write the kernel in
even-odd order as
##{K=\begin{pmatrix}5\bbI&C^{\mathsf T}\\C&5\bbI\end{pmatrix}.}
Put
##{M=25\bbI -C^{\mathsf T}C.}
Its even-even inverse block is #{5M^{-1}}:
eliminating the odd variable in
#{5u+C^{\mathsf T}v=f}, #{Cu+5v=0} gives
#{Mu=5f}. Every kernel is invertible by
\ref{fdip-00U7}, and #{\det K=\det M} by
\ref{fdip-00UA}.}

\p{The typed insertion formula of \ref{fdip-00WG}
therefore gives the determinant-weighted coefficient
##{-\det K\,(K^{-1})_{y,x}
 =-5\adjugate(M)_{1,0}
 =5\det N=Q(a,b,c,d,e).}
Here the degree-zero site order is
#{00,10,01,11}. The adjugate entry deletes row zero
and column one and carries cofactor sign
#{(-1)^{0+1}=-1}; this cancels the barred-first
minus sign. The polynomial is \ref{fdip-00X8}.}

\p{Every nonconstant squarefree word cancels in the
sum over the #{32} sign assignments, by pairing the
two choices of a letter it contains. The dressed
pair is gauge invariant by \ref{fdip-00WF}, so the
orbit size #{8} of \ref{fdip-00UA} gives numerator
#{8\cdot32\cdot412470750}.
The same reasoning gives
#{Z=8\cdot32\cdot35803094657}.
Division gives the first displayed value. For the
loop #{L_1=a}, the coefficient of #{a} in the
determinant polynomial gives the second value,
as already computed in \ref{fdip-00UA}.}
